{"t":"Lifesteal","s":"lifesteal-9d82a","k":"outro","i":"assets/wiki/Lifesteal_a214d2.png","q":2,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-twbox2 pi-layout-default\" role=\"region\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Lifesteal</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">12.00.7695<br/>December 03, 2018<br/>Winter Update 2018</span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"status\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Status</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Active</div>\n</div>\n</aside>\n<figure class=\"thumb show-info-icon\" style=\"width: 180px\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"> <img alt=\"Lifesteal being used in the fight against . The sparks effect appears on all players and between them, but it has is no specific geometry.\" class=\"thumbimage\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Lifesteal_a214d2.png\" width=\"180\"/> <figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> <svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg> <p class=\"caption\">Lifesteal being used in the fight against <a href=\"#/wiki/Alptramun\">Alptramun</a>. The sparks effect appears on all players and between them, but it has is no specific geometry.</p> </figcaption> </figure>\n<p><b>Lifesteal</b> is a special type of Creature Spell used by some bosses. The Lifesteal is not only a direct nor an area attack, but rather depends on the positioning of the players near the boss. It seems to be used on a target, but it will \"spread\" to players that are near each other, resembling a chain effect. As the name suggests, the damage dealt by Life Steal is returned to the caster as health, so it can be seen as the creatures' version of the Vampirism (Life Leech) Imbuement, but specific to one attack. \n</p><p>Similar to <a href=\"#/wiki/Damage%20Reflection\">Damage Reflection</a>, the health regenerated by the creature will not necessarily be the same as the damage taken by the player, because Lifesteal has a fixed percentage of efficiency (for example, 150%). It's also important to note that only the damage caused directly to health is recovered as Lifesteal, so even though those using <a href=\"#/wiki/Magic%20Shield\">Magic Shield</a> will also take damage, this damage does not heal the boss. \n</p><p>It seems to be possible to avoid the Lifesteal by standing far from other players in the same room, thus this should be tried when possible in order to minimize the damage taken and the boss healing. \n</p><p>The following messages appears on the server log when Lifesteal is used:\n</p><p><span class=\"tibiatext tibiawhite\">Creature healed itself for X hitpoints (lifesteal).</span><br/>\n<span class=\"tibiatext tibiawhite\">Player loses Y hitpoints due to an attack by creature.</span>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-List_of_Creatures_that_use_Lifesteal\">List of Creatures that use Lifesteal</span></h2>\n<p><b>Note</b>: Even though some bosses' summons also use this spell, only bosses are displayed here for simplicity.\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">Exp</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">HP</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">Max. Damage</th><th style=\"font-size: small;\">Loot</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 100px; text-align: center\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Alptramun\"><img alt=\"Alptramun\" class=\"mw-file-element\" 